response:
Incorporating graphene oxide (GO) into the matrix of polyethylene (PE) nanocomposites significantly improves their mechanical properties. The presence of GO nanosheets in the polymer matrix can enhance the overall strength and stiffness of the material. This is due to the high aspect ratio and large surface area of GO, which can provide a large support area for the polymer chains, as well as form strong hydrogen bonding interactions with the polymer. The resulting nanocomposite exhibits the following improvements:  
1. **Increased tensile strength and strain break-off strain** – GO can effectively pull the polymer chains fromeinander, resulting in increased resistance to deformation.  
2. **Improved stiffness and modulus of elasticity** – The stiffness of the nanocomposite is enhanced due to the rigid GO nanosheets inhibiting the polymer chain mobility.  
3. **Enhanced fracture strength and toughness** – GO can absorb energy during fracture, increasing the overall toughness of the nanocomposite.  

Thus, graphene oxide is an effective reinforcement for improving the mechanical properties of polyethylene-based nanocomposites.  

\boxed{
\begin{aligned}
&\text{1. Tensile strength and strain break-off strain improvement} \\
&\text{2. Increased stiffness and modulus} \\
&\text{3. Enhanced fracture strength and toughness}
\end{aligned}
}

